# Files whose merge conflicts are two branches each adding lines: keep both sides' lines (git's built-in `union`
# merge) instead of stopping at a conflict. It applies to local merges (`git merge`, tools/sync-pr.mjs resolves the same
# way for the rest); GitHub's own "Update branch" may not honour it. Not for a file where order or commas matter
# (quality.baseline.json), and the tests still say if both sides' lines together are wrong (a number used twice).
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
docs/MEMORY.md merge=union
src/engine/snapshot.txt merge=union
